<Project>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!-- A NuGet audit advisory of moderate, high or critical severity (NU1902, NU1903, NU1904) fails the
         build, so one cannot be scrolled past. In epic 14 the Aspire trial build printed 30 of them
         (critical on Aspire.Dashboard.Sdk, high on the hosting packages), nobody read them, and ADR-019 then
         pinned the vulnerable version. PR 3 hit it and ADR-020 replaced the pin. NU1901 (low) stays a
         warning. The price is that a new advisory on a package already in use will fail a build some
         morning. That is the point. Bump the package, or write an ADR for keeping it. The list is appended to and
         never replaced, as the core does for RS0030, and NuGetAuditMode is already all for net10.0, so the
         transitive packages, where the Aspire advisories were, are audited too. -->
    <WarningsAsErrors>$(WarningsAsErrors);NU1902;NU1903;NU1904</WarningsAsErrors>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
